xt":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degeneracy d."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MaximalCliques","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols":{"type":"topic","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","title":"GraphProtocols","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/maximalCliques()":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximalCliques()","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximalcliques()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every maximal clique once, lazily, each in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order; see "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MaximalCliques"},{"type":"text","text":" for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order. Self-loops and parallel edges are ignored, and an isolated vertex is a clique of one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(NetworkX "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"find_cliques"},{"type":"text","text":", igraph "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximal_cliques"},{"type":"text","text":", JGraphT’s Bron–Kerbosch finders)."}],"type":"topic","title":"maximalCliques()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"maximalCliques"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":